    actions: [
      { rank:1, emoji:'📈', text:'Progressive overload — add weight, reps, or sets every 1–2 weeks. This is the single most important variable for hypertrophy.' },
      { rank:2, emoji:'🍗', text:'Eat in a caloric surplus of 200–300 cal/day. Target 0.8–1g protein per lb of bodyweight. Without enough fuel, muscle growth stalls.' },
      { rank:3, emoji:'🏋️', text:'Train each muscle 2×/week. Meta-analyses consistently show twice-weekly frequency outperforms once-weekly for hypertrophy.' },
      { rank:4, emoji:'😴', text:'Sleep 8–9 hours. Growth hormone peaks during deep sleep — this is when muscle is actually built.' },
      { rank:5, emoji:'⏸️', text:'Allow 48–72 hours recovery between sessions for the same muscle group. Training a sore muscle before it recovers is counterproductive.' },
