      { rank:2, emoji:'📊', text:'Periodise your training. Linear or wave periodisation (gradually increasing load over 4–8 week cycles with deload weeks) prevents plateau.' },
      { rank:3, emoji:'🎯', text:'Focus on compound movements: squat, deadlift, bench, row, press. These train the most muscle simultaneously and produce the greatest strength transfer.' },
      { rank:4, emoji:'⏱️', text:'Rest 2–5 minutes between heavy sets. Insufficient rest means the next set uses a fatigued nervous system — you train weakness, not strength.' },
      { rank:5, emoji:'😴', text:'Deload every 4–6 weeks. A planned week of reduced volume allows supercompensation — you come back stronger.' },
    ],
  },
